                "text": [
                    "Global Issues",
                    "How does it specifically affect this country ?",
                    "Global human rights issues affect Australia in several ways. When people face persecution, discrimination, or the loss of basic freedoms in their own home countries, many seek refuge elsewhere. Australia receives refugees from countries experiencing human rights violations, which means Australia plays a key role in providing Human protection and support. Australia also works with international organizations and other countries to promote human rights and advocate for equality and justice worldwide. Therefore, human rights issues are not only a concern for the countries where they happen, but also for countries that try to help, like Australia and several others, including Canada. However, this drive to help people who are facing persecution in their home countries \u2014 where the Universal Declaration of Human Rights is being violated\u2014 has led to challenges within Australia itself. It has become one of the most persistent social, economic, and political issues in Australia, leading the majority of Australians to believe that the current level of immigration is too high. This has contributed to many further issues, such as a housing and rental crisis. Hospitals, public transport networks, and schools \u2014 particularly in major capital cities like Sydney and Melbourne, where migrants heavily cluster \u2014 are under extreme strain."
                ],
