                "text": [
                    "Brief Background on T\u00fcrkiye",
                    "T\u00fcrkiye, which goes by the official name of the Republic of T\u00fcrkiye, sits in the space between Europe and Asia. It's got Greece and Bulgaria to the west, Syria and Iraq to the south, and Iran beyond that. Then there's the Mediterranean, Aegean, and Black seas lapping at its shores too.\r\rWith over 85 million people,T\u00fcrkiye is home to quite a few folks. Ankara's the capital, but Istanbul's the biggest city by far. Most people speak Turkish, and their culture shows influences from the old Ottoman Empire, as well as the Middle East, Central Asia, and Europe.\r\rT\u00fcrkiye has a varied landscape\u2014from mountains to forests, to flat coastal areas. To match that, their economy thrives on different things like farming, tourism, making stuff in factories, and trade."
                ],
